{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at","id":411035,"title":"What are Solars Best At?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-18T21:54:03-08:00","id":411035,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What are Solars Best At?","content":"What are Solars Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Lunars Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Sidereals Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Dragon-Blooded Best At?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T21:56:50-08:00","id":411059,"title":"","content":"I can tell you what Lunars are <i>best</i> at. Adaptability. <br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at team play. <br /> <br /> Solars are best at skills. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are best at the slightly weird effects, being subtle perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:17:21-08:00","id":411067,"title":"","content":"Solars are best at sucking everyone around them into their story.<br /> Lunars are best at fitting themselves perfectly into whatever sort of story they find themselves in.<br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at ensemble-cast stories.<br /> Sidereals are best at retcons and stories that occasionally get weirdly meta.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:21:35-08:00","id":411069,"title":"","content":"I'd say solars are best at narrow focus. They are the best at their narrow focus but they meant to be leaders and slayers of primordial. They were designed to be a well aimed surgical strike not carpet bombing, thats what sidereals and dragonblooded are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:25:45-08:00","id":411073,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are definitely not carpet bombers. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:30:51-08:00","id":411075,"title":"","content":"Solars excel at imposing their will on the world bluntly. They will beat you with their fists and build cities on your grave. Solar Xerses wields the largest army mankind has every seen.<br /> <br /> Lunars excel at adapting to the world and carving a niche. They'll dodge your fist so you lose balance and hit a pole - and will infest your cities with bloodlines that you can't even tell are superior to mere men. Lunar Leonidas lets the Wolf lunge at him - and turns its strength against the beast, killing it.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded excel at team work. They'll figure out some neat combos and later claim your cities because you're a shitty tyrant. You might be the bigger kid on the block, but they're a small gang that will jump you.<br /> <br /> Sidereals excel at.... well if they told us, they'd have to kill us. : / I don't trust them tho.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:40:29-08:00","id":411100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411073#post411073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are definitely not carpet bombers. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>They are if you know how to use multiple invocations of low impact large area blessings and curses through fate altering.<br /> <br /> Plus you can literally take a city and move it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:43:14-08:00","id":411103,"title":"","content":"Solars are best at leading from the front.<br /> <br /> Lunars are best at leading from the side.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are best at leading from behind.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at leading from within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:45:22-08:00","id":411104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411067#post411067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are best at sucking everyone around them into their story.<br /> Lunars are best at fitting themselves perfectly into whatever sort of story they find themselves in.<br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at ensemble-cast stories.<br /> Sidereals are best at retcons and stories that occasionally get weirdly meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>*two thumbs up*<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411103#post411103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are best at leading from the front.<br /> <br /> Lunars are best at leading from the side.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are best at leading from behind.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at leading from within.</div> </div> </div> </div>You too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T22:59:23-08:00","id":411114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411075#post411075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars excel at imposing their will on the world bluntly. They will beat you with their fists and build cities on your grave. Solar Xerses wields the largest army mankind has every seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just about the entire Night Caste would like to have a word with you.<br /> <br /> (I wanted to throw the Eclipse Caste in there as well, but... well, the most famous and celebrated Eclipse Caste in Creation ever made his reputation, not via epic diplomacy and deal-making, but by stringing a guy along until he could sucker-punch him and then flew away laughing. So... yeah.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:13:43-08:00","id":411120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411114#post411114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I wanted to throw the Eclipse Caste in there as well, but... well, the most famous and celebrated Eclipse Caste in Creation ever made his reputation, not via epic diplomacy and deal-making, but by stringing a guy along until he could sucker-punch him and then flew away laughing. So... yeah.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think the Eclipse Caste who decides to go all Illuminati Master would end up being famous or celebrated, would he? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:23:24-08:00","id":411124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411114#post411114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just about the entire Night Caste would like to have a word with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>As soon as their animas flare, they become GIANT BALL OF GLOWING NINJA.<br /> <br /> &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> Lunar ninja could stealth easier (in-and-out as a hummingbird) and if they start glowing, True Form (bird!) and fly out of there.<br /> <br /> Sidereal ninja manipulated the Lunar and Solar ninjas to be there in the first place. No one knows about Sidereal ninja.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial ninja have an elemental ninja style and probably own the property (so the Patricians merely pretend not to see them).<br /> <br /> TLDR: Solars are the most obvious ninjas when it comes to ninjaing. Their idea of stealth ends up being <i><b><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">&quot;YOU DON'T SEE ME BECAUSE I'M GONNA BLIND YOU WITH HOW RADIANTLY AWESOME I AM, TIL I'M NAUGHT BUT A SILHOUETTE - BUT NO WORRIES, YOU CAN RECOGNIZE MY ANIMA BANNER AS MY CALLING CARD, I AM THAAAAAAT AWESOME&quot;</span></b></i>.<br /> <br /> Solar Ninjas are the Malfeas of Ninjas. : /<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411114#post411114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I wanted to throw the Eclipse Caste in there as well, but... well, the most famous and celebrated Eclipse Caste in Creation ever made his reputation, not via epic diplomacy and deal-making, but by stringing a guy along until he could sucker-punch him and then flew away laughing. So... yeah.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, go ahead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &lt;3 No one is holding you back.<br /> <br /> Also, Solars - capable of using social-charms to inflict Aggravated damage to creatures of darkness. A <i>social charm</i> that lets them melt your face off with Aggravated damage. In DotFA, they have a higher-Essence charm that lets them declare you a CoD........ so first they condemn you at will, <b>then</b> they can bludgeon your mind, and <b>then</b> they can melt your face off. <b>With social charms</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:30:13-08:00","id":411130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at#post411035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Solars Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Lunars Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Sidereals Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Dragon-Blooded Best At?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever they want to be best at<br /> <br /> Whatever you don't want them to be best at<br /> <br /> Whatever you least expect them to be best at<br /> <br /> Whatever their weakest link is best at","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:59:30-08:00","id":411162,"title":"","content":"Solars specialize<br /> <br /> Lunars adapt<br /> <br /> Sidereals trick the world<br /> <br /> Dragonblood cooperate<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411124#post411124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As soon as their animas flare, they become GIANT BALL OF GLOWING NINJA.<br /> <br /> &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> Lunar ninja could stealth easier (in-and-out as a hummingbird) and if they start glowing, True Form (bird!) and fly out of there.<br /> <br /> Sidereal ninja manipulated the Lunar and Solar ninjas to be there in the first place. No one knows about Sidereal ninja.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial ninja have an elemental ninja style and probably own the property (so the Patricians merely pretend not to see them).<br /> <br /> TLDR: Solars are the most obvious ninjas when it comes to ninjaing. Their idea of stealth ends up being <i><b><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">&quot;YOU DON'T SEE ME BECAUSE I'M GONNA BLIND YOU WITH HOW RADIANTLY AWESOME I AM, TIL I'M NAUGHT BUT A SILHOUETTE - BUT NO WORRIES, YOU CAN RECOGNIZE MY ANIMA BANNER AS MY CALLING CARD, I AM THAAAAAAT AWESOME&quot;</span></b></i>.<br /> <br /> Solar Ninjas are the Malfeas of Ninjas. : /<br /> <br /> Please, go ahead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &lt;3 No one is holding you back.<br /> <br /> Also, Solars - capable of using social-charms to inflict Aggravated damage to creatures of darkness. A <i>social charm</i> that lets them melt your face off with Aggravated damage. In DotFA, they have a higher-Essence charm that lets them declare you a CoD........ so first they condemn you at will, <b>then</b> they can bludgeon your mind, and <b>then</b> they can melt your face off. <b>With social charms</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Night Caste Anima hides your identity, for one. For another, you can keep your anima from flaring in the first place","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T02:15:56-08:00","id":411228,"title":"","content":"Solars: Anything.<br /> <br /> Lunars: Argument provoking.<br /> <br /> Sidereals: Suffering.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded: Aristocracy-ing.<br /> <br /> <br /> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T04:30:07-08:00","id":411307,"title":"","content":"No mention of Alchemicals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T05:09:33-08:00","id":411321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411307#post411307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mention of Alchemicals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemicals are the best at being generally amazing and utterly ridiculously awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T05:53:47-08:00","id":411345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411104#post411104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411067#post411067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are best at sucking everyone around them into their story.<br /> Lunars are best at fitting themselves perfectly into whatever sort of story they find themselves in.<br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at ensemble-cast stories.<br /> Sidereals are best at retcons and stories that occasionally get weirdly meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>*two thumbs up*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411103#post411103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are best at leading from the front.<br /> <br /> Lunars are best at leading from the side.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are best at leading from behind.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are best at leading from within.</div> </div> </div> </div>You too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to second Sunder's thumbs up to both Wise Old Guru and Arcanus Dicere. I think both descriptions are spot on. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:24:30-08:00","id":411408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411124#post411124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TLDR: Solars are the most obvious ninjas when it comes to ninjaing. Their idea of stealth ends up being <i><b><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">&quot;YOU DON'T SEE ME BECAUSE I'M GONNA BLIND YOU WITH HOW RADIANTLY AWESOME I AM, TIL I'M NAUGHT BUT A SILHOUETTE - BUT NO WORRIES, YOU CAN RECOGNIZE MY ANIMA BANNER AS MY CALLING CARD, I AM THAAAAAAT AWESOME&quot;</span></b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet they're also the ones that, if they wish, never get to glow at all. Also remember what the devs mentioned about the Mute keyword. Wanna bet how most charms for not being seen are mute in the first place and thus don't flare up with peripheral motes even if you don't use anything to suppress it?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:26:54-08:00","id":411411,"title":"","content":"What are Solars Best At? Leading<br /> <br /> What are Lunars Best At? Enforcing <br /> <br /> What are Sidereals Best At? Advising <br /> <br /> What are Dragon-Blooded Best At? Following<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:28:31-08:00","id":411413,"title":"","content":"Am I speaking in Hieroglyphics? &gt;_&lt;<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411162#post411162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Night Caste Anima hides your identity, for one. For another, you can keep your anima from flaring in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't exactly deny this, did I? I was just commenting on method. It's pretty obvious:<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals </b>have<b> Arcane Fate</b> and <b>Resplendent Destinies </b>on their side. <i>The setting itself</i> bends to not see you and then forget you.<br /> <br /> <b>Lunars </b>have <b>Shapeshifting</b>. I can get <i>a lot further</i>, with <i>less investment</i>, sneaking into places as a critter - thereby avoid anima display altogether. Hell, my old No Moon anima banner has things like &quot;gains a <b>shadowy penumbra</b> that causes attackers who<b> cannot see</b> through <b>darkness</b> to suffer....a penalty.&quot; and &quot;is just as obvious as any other flaring Lunar, but the light springs from the silver edge of her anima and <b>the shadow within remains</b>&quot;. The Changing Moon anima banner also is pure &quot;illusion&quot; and &quot;shifting light and shadows&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Solars </b>(and yes, specifically Night Castes) end up looking like silhouettes against their own anima. &quot;Once the Solar spends 11-15 motes of Essence, though she is just as obvious as any other Exalt, her features are completely obscured by her anima display. Thus, assuming one of them saw her prior to her anima flaring, witnesses would be aware a Solar had been in their midst, but not her identity.&quot;<br /> <br /> So as before: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Their idea of stealth ends up being </i><i><b><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">&quot;YOU DON'T SEE ME BECAUSE I'M GONNA BLIND YOU WITH HOW RADIANTLY AWESOME I AM, TIL I'M NAUGHT BUT A SILHOUETTE - BUT NO WORRIES, YOU CAN RECOGNIZE MY ANIMA BANNER AS MY CALLING CARD, I AM THAAAAAAT AWESOME&quot;</span></b></i><i>.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Solar Ninjas are the Malfeas of Ninjas. : /</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Incidentally, this kind of banter might be great at figuring out their differences. o_o Heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:31:16-08:00","id":411415,"title":"","content":"Solars: Startups<br /> Lunars: Mergers &amp; Acquisitions<br /> Sidereals: Synergistic Managment<br /> Dragonblooded: Hostile Takeovers, Branding","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T06:40:53-08:00","id":411423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411413#post411413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Solars </b>(and yes, specifically Night Castes) end up looking like silhouettes against their own anima. &quot;Once the Solar spends 11-15 motes of Essence, though she is just as obvious as any other Exalt, her features are completely obscured by her anima display. Thus, assuming one of them saw her prior to her anima flaring, witnesses would be aware a Solar had been in their midst, but not her identity.&quot;<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this kind of banter might be great at figuring out their differences. o_o Heh.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bmkxsQnNujI\" data-code=\"bmkxsQnNujI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bmkxsQnNujI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:12:28-08:00","id":411446,"title":"","content":"What are Solars Best At? Leading <br /> <br /> What are Lunars Best At? Enforcing<br /> <br /> What are Sidereals Best At? Advising <br /> <br /> What are Dragon-Blooded Best At? Following","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:34:51-08:00","id":411464,"title":"","content":"I made a handy little chart:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/15xy7EY.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411423#post411423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bmkxsQnNujI\" data-code=\"bmkxsQnNujI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/bmkxsQnNujI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I like you bunches right now. Bunches. :3 I was looking up this art style and somehow forgot Samurai Jack. Squeeeeeeeeeeeeeee<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T07:57:38-08:00","id":411508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411120#post411120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't think the Eclipse Caste who decides to go all Illuminati Master would end up being famous or celebrated, would he? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, but Eclipse Caste Metternich probably would be, at least among their peers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously, I completely understand that signature First Age Solars more or less had to be representations of what happens when a high-essence elder Solar really wallows in the Great Curse and their own hubris, but at least the Hierophant makes sense as a Zenith qua Zenith. Desus honestly never seemed like much of a deal-maker or diplomat, and his most famous action was just... punching someone's lights out.<br /> <br /> I stand by my statement that the Night Caste aren't blunt instruments, tho.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be the annoying one in this thread and take a more grossly mechanical, rather than narrative, look at these questions, mostly because people who are far more clever than I am have already give all the best koan-like answers and why chase success?<br /> <br /> Also too, to define terms: there's a difference between &quot;this what $EXALT_TYPE is best at,&quot; and &quot;$EXALT_TYPE is <i>the</i> best at this.&quot; I'm gonna assume hippocreme was asking the former and not the latter, although in the specific case of Solar-equivalents they're rather intertwined. So with that in mind...<br /> <br /> Solars are the best at <i>anything</i>, although any individual Solar cannot be the best at <i>everything</i>. They have a large resource bank and cost-efficient access to applications of Essence that are just straight-up superior to everyone else. There are exceptions to this, I remember a lot of 1e Sidereal chicanery involving Blade of the Battle Maiden and Joy in Adversity Stance for example, but for the most part if a Solar stakes out a competency and pursues it, it won't just be the thing they personally are best at, they will be <i>the best </i>at it period everything else being equal.<br /> <br /> Lunars are, as has been said, the best at adaptability. In actual practice on a real table, what this boils down to is that shapeshifting is the swiss army knife of powers. Assuming other forms is very cheap and very useful and very powerful, and a creative, adaptive player can use that hammer to drive in every nail they see, especially because that hammer is also a wrench and a screwdriver. They're also the best at remaining themselves; their immunity to Shaping effects is not always relevant but it is <i>complete</i>; no force in the setting can force a Lunar to stop being a Lunar short of, well, killing them.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are tricky; I'm probably going to spend more words on them than the other three combined. First, I'm going to say that in this context, I don't think Sidereals are best being martial artists. That's the obvious first answer for their mechanical table strength, right, martial arts? And I don't think it is so. They may be the best martial artists, but I don't think that's what they themselves are best at.<br /> <br /> So what are they best at? Giving it some though, I would have to say that Sidereals are equally best at two things; defining or ignoring the terms of reality, and remotely managing all manner of... stuff. Sidereal mechanical effects tend to function around &quot;Sidereal decides that X is true, not Y, and behold, it is so.&quot; These usually happen through a sheer act of will, or occasionally (Neighborhood Relocation Scheme) require action that one suspects is a metaphor for what's actually happening. Any other Exalt who wants Y to be untrue and X to be true has to engage in what we'd recognize as logical, observable steps to get there. A Sidereal just thinks about it, expends motes, and it <i>happens</i>.<br /> <br /> Their ability to do this is heavily circumscribed by both the narrowness of their Charms and the closed charmset, but it is definitely what they are best at. Their other major competency is the ability to lay ongoing effects on the world via Astrology and then walk away and leave those effects running without needing to either commit essence or constantly monitor and tweak things. They can just slap penalties and bonuses (as well as other stuff) onto people, places, and things, and then stroll away and leave it running. This can be wickedly hard to use at the table (Sidereal Astrology rules have broken strong men) but I would have to say it is definitely a &quot;best at&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are also slightly tricky. I don't actually think that what they themselves are best at is synergy, although they're clearly better at that than any other Exalt type. What I have to say is that they're best at being basically competent.<br /> <br /> No, really. Best at competence. Hear me out! Dragon-Blooded have dirt cheap basic dice-adders/Excellencies. They can leverage specialties into their dice pools in an efficient manner as well. Your &quot;default&quot; Dragon-Blooded is going to have access to a lot of equipment, artifact and otherwise, to help them do whatever it is they like, and they're probably plugged into a support network of some sort as well. As befits their status as soldiers, what Dragon-Blooded are best at is just throwing lots and lots of dice at a problem until the problem goes away. They can do that very cheaply and very well, better than anything else they can do, really. So that's what I'm going to say they're best at.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:45:55-08:00","id":411614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at#post411035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Solars Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Lunars Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Sidereals Best At?<br /> <br /> What are Dragon-Blooded Best At?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doing.<br /> <br /> Becoming.<br /> <br /> Arranging.<br /> <br /> Joining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:00:06-08:00","id":411706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411120#post411120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't think the Eclipse Caste who decides to go all Illuminati Master would end up being famous or celebrated, would he? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats why oddly enough The Silver Prince is a great example of an eclipse. He's got a persona to be all charismatic and inspiring, while in truth he's making backroom deals and carefully hiding what the real ruler is like. Its alot like the idea of a puppet ruler, just the puppet is also him so he can still make use of all those high essence charms and ensure actual competant leadership so no one questions things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T11:30:36-08:00","id":411820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411413#post411413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I speaking in Hieroglyphics? &gt;_&lt;I didn't exactly deny this, did I? I was just commenting on method. It's pretty obvious:<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals </b>have<b> Arcane Fate</b> and <b>Resplendent Destinies </b>on their side. <i>The setting itself</i> bends to not see you and then forget you.<br /> <br /> <b>Lunars </b>have <b>Shapeshifting</b>. I can get <i>a lot further</i>, with <i>less investment</i>, sneaking into places as a critter - thereby avoid anima display altogether. Hell, my old No Moon anima banner has things like &quot;gains a <b>shadowy penumbra</b> that causes attackers who<b> cannot see</b> through <b>darkness</b> to suffer....a penalty.&quot; and &quot;is just as obvious as any other flaring Lunar, but the light springs from the silver edge of her anima and <b>the shadow within remains</b>&quot;. The Changing Moon anima banner also is pure &quot;illusion&quot; and &quot;shifting light and shadows&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Solars </b>(and yes, specifically Night Castes) end up looking like silhouettes against their own anima. &quot;Once the Solar spends 11-15 motes of Essence, though she is just as obvious as any other Exalt, her features are completely obscured by her anima display. Thus, assuming one of them saw her prior to her anima flaring, witnesses would be aware a Solar had been in their midst, but not her identity.&quot;<br /> <br /> So as before: [/I]<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this kind of banter might be great at figuring out their differences. o_o Heh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, A night caste's anima doesn't flare if they don't want it to - they just need to spend extra motes. That means that the only reason to have a night caste's anima flare like that is in the middle of a raised alarm/escape scene where stealth is no longer an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T12:23:34-08:00","id":411865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411820#post411820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, A night caste's anima doesn't flare if they don't want it to - they just need to spend extra motes. That means that the only reason to have a night caste's anima flare like that is in the middle of a raised alarm/escape scene where stealth is no longer an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well their anima flare also obscures their identity. So if they ever get caught and can't re-stealth, the best option for them is to flare - sure they out themselves as Anathema, but nobody knows what they look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:05:15-08:00","id":411971,"title":"","content":"I wonder how one would go about accommodating a player that wants to play out a Yakitate Japan character - making food so spicy it heats itself to furnace tempteratures, or so minty that it freezes waves solid when thrown at a tsunami. (it's basically the only way to get said player to try out Exalted.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:06:32-08:00","id":411972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411865#post411865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well their anima flare also obscures their identity. So if they ever get caught and can't re-stealth, the best option for them is to flare - sure they out themselves as Anathema, but nobody knows what they look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. &lt;3 Someone gets it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Again, A night caste's anima doesn't flare if they don't want it to - they just need to spend extra motes. That means that the only reason to have a night caste's anima flare like that is in the middle of a raised alarm/escape scene where stealth is no longer an option.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I never said Solars can't be ninjas.<br /> <br /> I'm saying Sidereals and Lunars have an easier time of it -- it's a lot cheaper to turn into a raiton and fly to a castle tower than it is to spend a few scenes (and using charms throughout) to approach the castle walls, bypass the gate, walk the streets unseen, dodge the traps you set off, etc, etc. Eat a Raiton and just fucking <i><b>fly</b></i> into a Shadowland unmolested.<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> &quot;Spend twice as much Essence on various charms&quot; (depleting your power) vs &quot;turn into a glowing bonfire so no one can see your face&quot; (the optimal, if funny, option) are too pretty hard choices when I could simply <i>shapeshift <b>once</b></i>(for a pittance) and move unmolested.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thats why oddly enough The Silver Prince is a great example of an eclipse. He's got a persona to be all charismatic and inspiring, while in truth he's making backroom deals and carefully hiding what the real ruler is like. Its alot like the idea of a puppet ruler, just the puppet is also him so he can still make use of all those high essence charms and ensure actual competant leadership so no one questions things. </div> </div> </div>What's odd about it?<br /> <br /> The Silver Prince has been hinted at being Desus / Swan's (the signature Eclipse) old incarnation. He has his game locked down tight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","user":"SachKreiosLucy4","date":". 02-19-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:06:49-08:00","id":411973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411971#post411971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how one would go about accommodating a player that wants to play out a Yakitate Japan character - making food so spicy it heats itself to furnace tempteratures, or so minty that it freezes waves solid when thrown at a tsunami. (it's basically the only way to get said player to try out Exalted.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifact weapon/cooking implement (giant butcher knife daiklaive, cooking twine with the stats of an artifact whip, meat-tenderizer goremaul, set of large artifact throwing needles that double as kebab skewers) + Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:13:36-08:00","id":411984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411972#post411972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a lot cheaper to turn into a <b>ration</b></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v209/clintonjeff/ZomgitsCj/Screenshot0030.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I know you meant raiton, but i had to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T13:33:11-08:00","id":412002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411984#post411984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v209/clintonjeff/ZomgitsCj/Screenshot0030.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>I know you meant raiton, but i had to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love you. &lt;3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T14:56:51-08:00","id":412125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=411865#post411865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well their anima flare also obscures their identity. So if they ever get caught and can't re-stealth, the best option for them is to flare - sure they out themselves as Anathema, but nobody knows what they look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, we covered that - I was addressing the argument that having your anima flare is terrible for stealth by pointing out that if your anima is flaring, stealth is already out the window as an option for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:01:36-08:00","id":412175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412125#post412125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know, we covered that - I was addressing the argument that having your anima flare is terrible for stealth by pointing out that if your anima is flaring, stealth is already out the window as an option for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, you quoted me.<br /> And I never said it was terrible for stealth.<br /> <br /> That's kind of like swinging your fists at a guy whose three blocks and fourteen years away from you.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>OP asked &quot;what are Solars&quot; (and Sidereals, and Lunars, and Terrestrials) &quot;best at&quot;.</li> <li>I responded (with typical, obvious, grandiose Solar god-king imagery) for what Solars excel at.</li> <li>Murcushio (probably in jest) responded by saying that the Night Caste &quot;would like to have a word with me&quot; (and then admitted to wanting to include Eclipse, only to realize that the most famous Eclipse in the setting literally solved a negotiation with a sucker-punch).</li> <li>I followed on the Night Caste example with their anima banner - <b>I like</b> (and was laughing at the absurd genius of it) that they continue to be stealthy, while glowing like a small explosion, a blackened silhouette against blinding light. It wasn't a criticism of Solar stealth - I admired the fact that they found a &quot;brute force&quot; way to depict a traditionally &quot;subtle, delicate&quot; thing (stealth).</li> <li>Thereafter there sprung up people trying to argue that a Night Caste could use their anima power to hide the banner, to quibble.</li> <li>My response <b>to that</b> was that Sidereals and Lunars can be stealthy -- <i>regardless of caste</i> -- <i>for a much reduced cost</i> -- and with <i>much less effort </i>-- <i>even with their animas flaring</i>.</li> </ol>Instead of addressing OP (with a broad, all-inclusive discussion and comparison of different splats and castes), some people have mistakenly confused this for a Solar Night-Caste Stealth thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:15:34-08:00","id":412185,"title":"","content":"Solars are best at Evocations, even their twisted forms aren't as good at it as they are (apparently artifacts hate death and yozi flavored essence or something).<br /> <br /> Lunars are best at turning into a god beast and biting your face off<br /> <br /> Sidereal are the best at working overtime<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded are best at using awesome elemental powers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T16:19:04-08:00","id":412186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412125#post412125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know, we covered that - I was addressing the argument that having your anima flare is terrible for stealth by pointing out that if your anima is flaring, stealth is already out the window as an option for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really.<br /> <br /> Anima flares, obscuring identity. You jump out a window onto a ledge, use Sun-Swallowing Method (or whatever it was called - the thing that lets you diminish your anima), and return to the darkness. Whoever caught you might not even know you were Anathema unless they case the Caste mark - you could be some kind of terrible spirit or something (but don't count on that).<br /> <br /> The moment might be spoiled by the entire endeavor might not be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:23:41-08:00","id":412227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at#post411035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Solars Best At?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are Lunars Best At? </div> </div> </div>Nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are Sidereals Best At? </div> </div> </div>Nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are Dragon-Blooded Best At? </div> </div> </div>Having lots of Exalts show up at your family reunion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:40:03-08:00","id":412242,"title":"","content":"I wonder, will Solar unparalleled excellence at Evocations be counterbalanced against Abyssal unparalleled excellence at Necromancy and Infernal at Sorcery?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"