an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:56:55-08:00","id":412250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412242#post412242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, will Solar unparalleled excellence at Evocations be counterbalanced against Abyssal unparalleled excellence at Necromancy and Infernal at Sorcery?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it even possible for Infernals to be better at sorcery? Solars already get Adamant Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:10:54-08:00","id":412278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412250#post412250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it even possible for Infernals to be better at sorcery? Solars already get Adamant Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously he's gonna houserule things at his table so Infernals get <i>Double</i> Adamant Circle, allowing them to cast &quot;Total<i>er</i> Annihilation,&quot; &quot;Unity of the Closed Fist + Shotgun,&quot; and &quot;Summon Yozi.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:26:14-08:00","id":412288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412250#post412250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it even possible for Infernals to be better at sorcery? Solars already get Adamant Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't impossible, the evocation tree that they gave us as a spoiler awhile back showed us how they were (at the time) ensuring that solars were the best at evocations even when another exalt could access adamant level evocations. One branch of the tree flat out had a solar charm as the pre-req to start learning it, meaning that even if another exalt could access adamant evocations they still couldn't get everything out of it a solar does. They could always do something similar with infernals and lock some adamant sorcery behind a big 'only for people with a certain GSP specific charm' sign.<br /> <br /> Of course, I really seriously doubt they are going to do that. But they totally could if they wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:40:30-08:00","id":412295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412227#post412227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Having lots of Exalts show up at your family reunion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>that's</i> hardly fair. Sidereals are currently world record holders for 'Most Solars Murdered In Least Amount Of Time'!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:44:35-08:00","id":412299,"title":"","content":"Nah, assuming you're talking about the Usurpation, the Dragon-Blooded have a higher kill count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:51:02-08:00","id":412303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412288#post412288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't impossible, the evocation tree that they gave us as a spoiler awhile back showed us how they were (at the time) ensuring that solars were the best at evocations even when another exalt could access adamant level evocations. One branch of the tree flat out had a solar charm as the pre-req to start learning it, meaning that even if another exalt could access adamant evocations they still couldn't get everything out of it a solar does. They could always do something similar with infernals and lock some adamant sorcery behind a big 'only for people with a certain GSP specific charm' sign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other splats could always have Call the Blade in their Charmsets as well. I doubt it, but it's possible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:55:58-08:00","id":412307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412250#post412250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it even possible for Infernals to be better at sorcery? Solars already get Adamant Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>My expectation is that, if you're looking at Sorcery as an entirely self-contained thing, Solars will be at least as good with any and all types of it as any other variety of Exalted. Full stop.* However, it is certainly possible that different Charmsets (or native Exalted capabilities) could have unique interactions with Sorcery, or may just be naturally synergistic with certain sorts of Sorcery spells, initiations, etc. For this reason, I'd probably say that I expect Solars will have the most potential for Sorcery overall, even as Abyssal and Infernal Sorcerous devotees** still have a leg up on them in places.<br /> <br /> * Though I still wouldn't be surprised if, say, the necromantic initiation path (or whathaveyou) made it hard/impossible to reach the pinnacle of its power if you aren't an Abyssal.<br /> ** And I certainly still expect some of this for members of other splats, mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412288#post412288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't impossible, the evocation tree that they gave us as a spoiler awhile back showed us how they were (at the time) ensuring that solars were the best at evocations even when another exalt could access adamant level evocations. One branch of the tree flat out had a solar charm as the pre-req to start learning it, meaning that even if another exalt could access adamant evocations they still couldn't get everything out of it a solar does. They could always do something similar with infernals and lock some adamant sorcery behind a big 'only for people with a certain GSP specific charm' sign.<br /> <br /> Of course, I really seriously doubt they are going to do that. But they totally could if they wanted to.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is an admittedly plausible interpretation, I can't agree with asserting it as the correct one. For starters, it assumes Evocation arrays are pretty rigid. From what we've heard, every character that picks up a given artifact can draw an entirely different set of Evocations from it.*** A given Solar who wields Volcano Cutter isn't necessarily going to see that Solar Charm prerequisite in her personal Evocation array. For a non-Solar character, it certainly wouldn't make sense to have a Charm she can't learn in her own array.**** If the splat in question has a Charm that works similar enough to Call the Blade, it's plausible that it could work as a substitute; the player could then use the array printed in the book with minimal alteration. All it means is that players of Solars -- the only splat written at the time -- can definitely just use the printed Evocation array straight out of the box. It's possible players of other splats may just have to do some retooling. Whether the non-Solar character can access Adamant level Evocations is a different matter.<br /> <br /> *** Within reason for the nature of the artifact and its relationship with the character, naturally. Firing magic rainbow lasers probably isn't kosher for a Frostmourne-like soulsteel daiklave, absent a good bit of creativity.<br /> **** Well, I guess it might, if it served a particular purpose in the nature of the character's relationship with the artifact. I don't know that too many players are going to like whatever statement that sends, though. At least not enough to deliberately pop or leave it in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T19:12:06-08:00","id":412322,"title":"","content":"Well, it seems like it would be trivially easy to homebrew that out of the system even for someone as mechanically illiterate as myself. Just say the solar only evocations are regular evocations that you don't need a solar charm to learn /done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T19:43:27-08:00","id":412343,"title":"","content":"In terms of rock bands:<br /> <br /> What are Solars best at? Lead Guitar<br /> <br /> What are Lunars best at? Rhythm Guitar<br /> <br /> What are Sidereals best at? Bass<br /> <br /> What are Dragon-Blooded best at? Drums","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r312/WuseMajor/t4q8xrt1_zps39b23a54.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/251-seifus","name":"Seifus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar251_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T19:52:42-08:00","id":412354,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who finds it appropriate how the Night Caste, the caste representative of &quot;Yeah, guys, the Sun isn't here&quot;, of the <i>Sun</i> Exalts, is somewhat the odd man out when it comes to how he does things?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412299#post412299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, assuming you're talking about the Usurpation, the Dragon-Blooded have a higher kill count.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depend on how you count kill-assists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:42:21-08:00","id":412519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412227#post412227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Having lots of Exalts show up at your family reunion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing that Sidereals and Lunars are best at? They have no clear strengths at all?<br /> <br /> Not even something like 'turn into an animal' or 'manipulate fate?'<br /> <br /> Also, being best at everything is the same as being best at nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-20-2015, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:53:15-08:00","id":412530,"title":"","content":"Solars are the best at making everyone else feel like sidekicks. <br /> <br /> Lunars are the best at side tracking threads.<br /> <br /> Sidereal are the second best at confusing people with their weird rules (Fair Folk beat them out there).<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded are the best at killing Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T01:30:16-08:00","id":412557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412519#post412519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing that Sidereals and Lunars are best at? They have no clear strengths at all?<br /> <br /> Not even something like 'turn into an animal' or 'manipulate fate?'<br /> <br /> Also, being best at everything is the same as being best at nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being pedantic is just as unhelpful as the people asking wrong-headed questions.<br /> <br /> I don't want my Exaltation to make me the best at anything. I want to make MYSELF the best at something (if that's what I want), and my Exaltation just helps me get there with greater or lesser degrees of challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T03:33:59-08:00","id":412593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412557#post412557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being pedantic is just as unhelpful as the people asking wrong-headed questions.<br /> <br /> I don't want my Exaltation to make me the best at anything. I want to make MYSELF the best at something (if that's what I want), and my Exaltation just helps me get there with greater or lesser degrees of challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry if you find my question wrong headed; I've enjoyed most of the responses and think some of them are insightful. I've also enjoyed reading people disagreeing about what each splat is best at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-20-2015, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T04:13:09-08:00","id":412623,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are best at manipulation..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T05:26:13-08:00","id":412648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412623#post412623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are best at manipulation..</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are best at keeping up Appearance(s)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T05:54:32-08:00","id":412659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412648#post412648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars are best at keeping up Appearance(s)</div> </div> </div> </div>With Dragon-Blooded being the best at asking &quot;are you being served?&quot; while Infernals are housed in faulty towers? (Don't talk about the Primordial War!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T06:18:04-08:00","id":412673,"title":"","content":"Thanks Holden.<br /> <br /> ITT: Dragonblooded are stronger than sidereals in 3e. This is deprotagonising to lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T06:34:13-08:00","id":412683,"title":"","content":"At the Olympics:<br /> <br /> Solars: Throw the farthest, swim the fastest. Win by excellence.<br /> <br /> Abyssals: Sap their strength and drown them. Win by default.<br /> <br /> Infernals: Screw this, I'll make my own Olympics! With blackjack! And hookers!<br /> <br /> Lunars: No matter which one seems to win, the Lunar wins. Mmmm, tasty!<br /> <br /> Sidereals: Pretend to participate. Place bets on everyone but yourself. Win ALL the bets.<br /> <br /> Dragonbloods: Win at nothing but Synchronized Swimming 40 centuries in a row.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T11:16:44-08:00","id":412953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412519#post412519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing that Sidereals and Lunars are best at? They have no clear strengths at all?<br /> <br /> Not even something like 'turn into an animal' or 'manipulate fate?'<br /> <br /> Also, being best at everything is the same as being best at nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what holden is saying is a slightly trick answer, if a lunar says &quot;im the best at changing into an animal&quot; then there wrong there the only ones who can do that, a solar doesn't have the capacity to perform the act, same with sids and fate manipulation, that's not what there the best at its what there unique &quot;thing&quot; is, everyone can do sorcery, but solars can do it the best, everyone can do martial arts so solars can get the top styles. but this doesn't supersede everything to do with the others unique mechanics .....or im reading to much into it and they just nerfed everyone else and gave all the cool toys to the solars :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T11:59:20-08:00","id":412977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>black orchid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412953#post412953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or im reading to much into it and they just nerfed everyone else and gave all the cool toys to the solars :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, Solars always had the most cool toys. Heck, a Solar who really wants to turn into an animal learns some largency charms and disguises himself as one - no one could tell the difference, and he could probably do any animal, not just those he ate. He'd have to find a way to mimic flight, but that's about it - he can even mimic strength and size just fine by being a solar athlete and contortionist. It's just that Solars had to focus on it (at the expense of other stuff), while Lunars got to do it out of the box, on top of whatever they actually choose to focus on.<br /> <br /> But that's not even the question. The (intended, as I understood it) question was <i>not</i> &quot;What can [Solars/Lunars/Sidereals/Dragon-Blooded] do better than all the other splats?&quot;.<br /> The actually intended question, as I understand it, was: &quot;What is the best/easiest/most natural way for a [Solars/Lunars/Sidereals/Dragon-Blooded] to express their abilities?&quot;<br /> (this is probably poorly phrased due to the fact how many interpretations &quot;best&quot; can have (&quot;the best way is always the one that's the most fun for the player&quot;), but I hope you get what I mean.)<br /> <br /> For a Solar, that is sheer excellence: Being the best at what they do, whatever they choose to do.<br /> For a Lunar, it's (I guess) being an universalist, focusing on their &quot;natural&quot; attributes over learned skills.<br /> For Sids, it's (I guess) pulling strings (both in fate and in the bureaus of heaven) and 'rigging the game' in their favour.<br /> For DBs, it's (I guess) numbers and team-play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T12:18:14-08:00","id":412987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412519#post412519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing that Sidereals and Lunars are best at? They have no clear strengths at all?<br /> <br /> Not even something like 'turn into an animal' or 'manipulate fate?'<br /> <br /> Also, being best at everything is the same as being best at nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) &quot;Strengths&quot; do not mean, &quot;to be the best at.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2.) What you cite are effectively methodologies rather than ends.<br /> <br /> A Lunar can certainly turn into a cat better than a Solar can, by and large, just by definition of what a Solar does and what a Lunar does.<br /> <br /> The question is WHY the Lunar just turned into a cat. Did they do it to sneak? Solar Stealth charms will outclass them. Did they do it to fight? Look at any Solar combat tree. <br /> <br /> But if you want to solve your problems by turning into a cat (unlike turning into a snake, it does sometimes help), and having the option to go bird, shark, or tyrant lizard, then being Lunar is <i>absolutely</i> for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T12:41:17-08:00","id":413037,"title":"","content":"Solars the best at anything that can be done (long term or short term) with a human making an Attribute+Ability roll. This includes things like Sorcery, Supernatural Martial Arts and Evocations, because these are things humans can do in Exalted's world.<br /> <br /> Lunars will never be as good at Solars at a given task, but they have attribute charms that let them improvise on the fly much more easily. Also Shapeshifting, I guess.<br /> <br /> Sidereals aren't as good as Lunars at adapting, nor can they match a Solar's raw talent, but they have several sideways abilities that are very hard to anticipate or counter, and can engineer the universe to conspire in their favor via Fate.<br /> <br /> Dragon Blood aren't as good at adapting as Lunars, can't match the sheer excellence of a Solar, and are incapable of engineering the universe like Sidereals, but working together in a team, they can match and overwhelm any of them when the chips are down.<br /> <br /> In short, when playing to their strengths, any given Exalt can accomplish any given task, it'll just be harder for some than others (sometimes <i>much</i> harder) because their strengths aren't suited for a specific task. This is generally easiest for Solars, as their strengths are the most broad and widely applicable (Attribute+Ability roll), and gets harder as you go down the list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:33:17-08:00","id":413124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412245#post412245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doubt it. In part because I don't know why Infernals would be better at Sorcery than Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought was that Sorcery being learned from the Yozi based on the forces they used to build Creation, their favored Exalts might have some advantages compared to the people who had to wring the information out of them or come up with the techniques on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/614-promethean-and-crossovers?p=1144#post1144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it even possible for Infernals to be better at sorcery? Solars already get Adamant Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking in terms of savings on mote costs, lower entry requirements, that sort thing rather than scaling up the power level. Not that they'd be achieving spells and sorcerous workings that a Solar couldn't, but they'd be getting there sooner and have an easier time of it once they do. But maybe the new Shintai system will be where Infernals shine, and they're on an even footing with regard to Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:40:52-08:00","id":413136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=412987#post412987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1.) &quot;Strengths&quot; do not mean, &quot;to be the best at.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a thread about what [Exalt_Type] is the best at.<br /> <br /> You could say that Hippokrene is best at wasting her time surfing online. That doesn't mean no one is better than me at it, that means it's what I'm best at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=413037#post413037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars will never be as good at Solars at a given task...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the question isn't &quot;What are Lunars better than anyone else at?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:45:17-08:00","id":413164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=413136#post413136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say that Hippokrene is best at wasting her time surfing online. That doesn't mean no one is better than me at it, that means it's what I'm best at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa, d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T14:55:29-08:00","id":413191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/411035-what-are-solars-best-at?p=413164#post413164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa, d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quick.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T15:41:10-08:00","id":413275,"title":"","content":"@Lunars: In my brief time with Lunars, I find that asking what they're the best at misses the point of being one. Lunars aren't the best at anything, because they're the generalists.<br /> <br /> A Twilight Sorcerer vs a Lunar Sorceress. The Solar's a better sorcerer, yes, but since he's specialized that's all he can use his charms for. The Lunar's charms are geared around her intelligence stat - she can plan a war, build a bridge, win a contest of wits, and numerous other things besides.<br /> <br /> ....... That's the idea, anyway &gt;.&gt; the mechanics leave a lot to be desired. But we knew that. (yay homebrew fixes!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}